WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.145 --> 00:00:17.669
year the children were especially proud of their contributions to Thanksgiving dinner.

2
00:00:17.689 --> 00:00:25.736
"My herbs made the stuffing really delicious," Nan said with her mouth full.

3
00:00:27.137 --> 00:00:32.985
Jack scooped another potato onto his plate and said, "These are the best potatoes I've ever eaten!"

4
00:00:33.005 --> 00:00:36.887
"Has everyone had some of my beans?"

5
00:00:37.447 --> 00:00:38.187
Nat asked.

6
00:00:38.207 --> 00:00:40.048
"Of course!"

7
00:00:40.388 --> 00:00:41.149
Tommy said.

8
00:00:41.169 --> 00:00:45.891
"You grew so many that Asia said we must all eat three helpings!"

9
00:00:45.911 --> 00:00:54.774
"The pies came from my giant pumpkin," Rob said, "and wait till you see—" "Hush!"

10
00:00:55.375 --> 00:00:58.236
Daisy said, giving her cousin a gentle swat.

11
00:00:59.252 --> 00:01:00.653
"It's a surprise!"

12
00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:05.395
But the professor had overheard them and was curious.

13
00:01:05.415 --> 00:01:11.899
"Daisy, I know you helped bake many pies, but Rob's pumpkin was enormous.

14
00:01:12.399 --> 00:01:13.940
What did you do with the rest of it?"

15
00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:19.223
"Well uh Daisy hesitated.

16
00:01:20.704 --> 00:01:24.005
Dan rescued Daisy by handing a bowl of nuts to Mr.

17
00:01:24.045 --> 00:01:26.427
Bauer. "Sir, try these!"

18
00:01:26.967 --> 00:01:33.662
The professor looked down the table, murmuring to Jo, "Everyone seems to be in on this secret except

19
00:01:33.762 --> 00:01:36.143
me, but I can wait."

20
00:01:38.204 --> 00:01:40.565
After dinner they all went for a long walk.

21
00:01:43.146 --> 00:01:47.528
Then they waited impatiently for the rest of the family to arrive: Mr.

22
00:01:47.568 --> 00:01:47.968
and Mrs.

23
00:01:48.028 --> 00:01:54.671
March, Aunt Meg and baby Josy, Uncle Laurie and Aunt Amy with Bess and a special guest.

24
00:01:54.691 --> 00:01:56.752
"Mr. Hyde!"

25
00:01:57.068 --> 00:02:00.509
Dan exclaimed, immediately recognizing the naturalist.

26
00:02:00.529 --> 00:02:03.650
"What are you doing here?"

27
00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:07.711
"I thought he'd like to see how well you're doing," Laurie said.

28
00:02:07.731 --> 00:02:10.072
"We're so proud of you."

29
00:02:11.052 --> 00:02:14.633
"What a fine, polite young man you've turned into," Mr.

30
00:02:14.693 --> 00:02:15.794
Hyde said to Dan.

31
00:02:18.094 --> 00:02:18.875
Dan and Mr.

32
00:02:18.915 --> 00:02:23.496
Hyde went to a parlor to talk until it was time for the evening's entertainment.

33
00:02:25.724 --> 00:02:32.768
Then everyone went into the schoolroom, where Jack amazed the audience by solving math problems in his head.

34
00:02:34.729 --> 00:02:38.471
Tommy won the spelling bee, and Dan performed gymnastics.

35
00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.255
a strong lad," Mr.

36
00:02:45.315 --> 00:02:46.615
Hyde said to the professor.

37
00:02:46.635 --> 00:02:51.458
"When I go to South America in a few years, I'd like to take him along."

38
00:02:53.479 --> 00:02:57.857
Overhearing that remark, Dan smiled, grateful to both Mr.

39
00:02:57.917 --> 00:02:59.118
Hyde and the Bauers.

40
00:02:59.138 --> 00:03:02.239
"Where did the other children go?"

41
00:03:02.619 --> 00:03:03.660
the professor asked.

42
00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.201
"Back here!"

43
00:03:07.441 --> 00:03:10.342
said a muffled voice behind a curtain made of blankets.

44
00:03:15.244 --> 00:03:18.286
said more voices amid lots of giggles.

45
00:03:19.906 --> 00:03:23.288
The curtain rose to reveal Bess as Cinderella.

46
00:03:24.284 --> 00:03:32.991
Dressed in a ragged pinafore, she sat before a cardboard fireplace, not moving until Daisy whispered loudly, "Now!"

47
00:03:33.932 --> 00:03:37.275
"Oh, I wish I could go to the ball!"

48
00:03:37.896 --> 00:03:38.856
Cinderella said.

49
00:03:40.638 --> 00:03:46.863
Laurie clapped enthusiastically for his daughter, and Amy whispered, "My little darling!"

50
00:03:46.883 --> 00:03:50.926
"You must not speak to me!"

51
00:03:51.507 --> 00:03:54.061
scolded Cinderella, looking at her parents.

52
00:03:55.682 --> 00:04:00.747
The back of the fireplace opened like a door, and Nan appeared as the fairy godmother.

53
00:04:02.028 --> 00:04:06.832
Dressed in a red cloak and pointed hat, she struggled to get through the opening.

54
00:04:06.852 --> 00:04:10.495
"You shall go to the ball!"

55
00:04:11.035 --> 00:04:14.918
the fairy godmother said, tapping Cinderella with her wand.

56
00:04:14.938 --> 00:04:21.584
"Now you must show my pretty dress," Cinderella said, tugging on her pinafore.

57
00:04:23.056 --> 00:04:25.957
"No, no," Nan said in her own voice.

58
00:04:25.977 --> 00:04:30.119
"First you say, 'How can I go in these rags?'"

59
00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:32.660
"Oh, that's right!"

60
00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:35.821
Cinderella said, and repeated Nan's words.

61
00:04:37.282 --> 00:04:43.765
With that, the fairy godmother unfastened Cinderella's pinafore to reveal a beautiful pink dress.

62
00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:50.968
She placed a crown on Cinderella's head and gave her silver paper slippers.

63
00:04:52.772 --> 00:04:54.433
"But you have no coach!"

64
00:04:55.034 --> 00:04:57.936
the fairy godmother declared, waving her wand.

65
00:04:59.357 --> 00:05:06.101
Cinderella was too busy admiring her slippers to say her next line, so Silas just leaped into action

66
00:05:06.202 --> 00:05:07.102
from backstage.

67
00:05:07.122 --> 00:05:09.003
"Ready, Daisy?"

68
00:05:09.304 --> 00:05:09.964
he whispered.

69
00:05:09.984 --> 00:05:20.892
"Push!" Suddenly four rats appeared, pulling a magnificent coach made from Rob's pumpkin and Teddy's wagon.

70
00:05:22.584 --> 00:05:27.926
As the coachman, Teddy helped Cinderella into the coach and squeezed in beside her.

71
00:05:29.027 --> 00:05:33.569
Cinderella waved to the audience, and that was the end of the first scene.

72
00:05:34.969 --> 00:05:40.052
In the ball scene, Rob played the prince while Nan and Daisy were the stepsisters.

73
00:05:41.812 --> 00:05:50.296
The prince and Cinderella danced and danced until finally Nan had to whisper, "Cinderella, drop your shoe!"

74
00:05:51.648 --> 00:05:52.948
"Oops, I forgot!"

75
00:05:53.389 --> 00:05:59.510
gasped Cinderella, taking off a slipper and planting it in the middle of the stage before running away.

76
00:06:01.471 --> 00:06:08.593
In the last scene, the prince and the coachman arrived with the slipper, which didn't fit the stepsisters—only

77
00:06:08.713 --> 00:06:13.034
Cinderella. "I'm the princess!"

78
00:06:13.554 --> 00:06:16.375
Cinderella announced, running over to her parents.

79
00:06:17.475 --> 00:06:19.276
"Didn't I do a good job?"

80
00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:22.562
"It was a beautiful play!"

81
00:06:22.862 --> 00:06:23.543
Laurie said.

82
00:06:23.563 --> 00:06:29.708
"And now I know what happened to the pumpkin," the professor said with a smile.

83
00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:35.393
Following the play, Nat played a sweet song on his violin.

84
00:06:37.855 --> 00:06:41.278
When he finished, he bowed to Jo, saying, "Mr.

85
00:06:41.318 --> 00:06:42.939
Laurence wrote that piece for you."

86
00:06:42.959 --> 00:06:48.104
"Oh, thank you, Laurie," Jo said.

87
00:06:49.172 --> 00:06:51.813
"You're the one who deserves thanks," Laurie said.

88
00:06:51.833 --> 00:06:54.393
"Look at what you've done for these children.

89
00:06:55.794 --> 00:07:00.535
Nat, Dan, and Nan—and the others—are all so much better and so full of promise.

90
00:07:01.976 --> 00:07:05.557
And after John died, you comforted the twins as if they were your own children.

91
00:07:06.977 --> 00:07:09.738
When Bess is old enough, I want her to go to Plumfield."

92
00:07:11.278 --> 00:07:13.079
Jo couldn't resist teasing him.

93
00:07:13.099 --> 00:07:18.120
"I thought you were unsure about boys and girls at school together."

94
00:07:19.968 --> 00:07:24.471
"Not anymore, and now you must excuse me for a moment," Laurie said, slipping away.

95
00:07:26.091 --> 00:07:31.294
He soon returned with all the children, who formed a circle around Jo and the professor.

96
00:07:33.615 --> 00:07:39.439
Together they sang a Thanksgiving song, and at the end, the circle tightened into a hug.

97
00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:47.023
There was one plant that had taken root in all of Plumfield's gardens this year, and that was

98
00:07:47.483 --> 00:07:47.683
love.
